.TH GLAZE-SETTINGS 1 "2026-11-10" "Glaze 0.1.0" "Glaze User Commands"
.SH NAME
glaze-settings \- the Glaze GTK4 settings application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glaze-settings
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glaze-settings
is intended to be Glaze's native settings application. Its first pages will
cover appearance (theme family, light/dark scheme, reduced motion, scaling),
the panel (position, thickness, auto-hide, clock format, labels) and the desktop
(wallpaper, icons). It will read and write the same versioned configuration as
every other Glaze surface and share the same design tokens, so a change made here
is reflected by the shell without a second source of truth.
.PP
.B IMPLEMENTATION STATUS:
not yet implemented. There is no
.B glaze-settings
crate, no
.B apps/glaze-settings
source tree and no executable in this repository snapshot. Until the
application lands, configuration is edited directly in
.BR ~/.config/glaze/config.toml ;
that file's schema
.RB ( glaze-common::config )
is implemented and unit-tested, including forward migration from older
versions, so hand-editing it is safe. The exact keys are documented in
.BR docs/user-guide.md .
.SH OPTIONS
None. No options exist yet.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Location of
.BR glaze/config.toml ,
which this application will read and write.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Required, as a GTK4 Wayland client.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown. Not reachable until the binary exists.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glaze (1),
.BR glaze-shell (1),
.BR glaze-session (1),
.BR glaze-service (1),
.BR glaze-compositor (1)
